          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Beginnings in Filmmaking</strong><br>\nSteven Spielberg was born on December 18, 1946, in Cincinnati, Ohio. He began making amateur films at a young age, which led to a short film called \"Amblin'\" catching the attention of Hollywood executives. This success landed him a deal with Universal Studios.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Prominence</strong><br>\nSpielberg quickly rose to prominence with \"Jaws\" (1975), which established him as a leading director and was a monumental success. This film set the standard for summer blockbusters and showcased Spielberg's knack for storytelling and tension-building.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Genre-Defining Works</strong><br>\nSpielberg's influence extended through various genres with hits like \"Close Encounters of the Third Kind\" (1977) and \"E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial\" (1982). These films, blending science fiction with deep humanism, captivated audiences worldwide and are considered classics.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
