          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Historical Narratives and Human Experience</strong><br>\nIn the 1990s, Spielberg directed several films that focused on historical narratives, such as \"Schindler's List\" (1993) and \"Saving Private Ryan\" (1998). These films were acclaimed for their storytelling, visual style, and portrayal of profound human experiences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Diversifying Creative Roles</strong><br>\nApart from directing, Spielberg has also produced numerous films and television series. He co-founded the studio DreamWorks SKG, further extending his influence in the entertainment industry and allowing him to foster new talent and ideas.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Technological Advancements in Film</strong><br>\nSpielberg has been at the forefront of using technology in film, employing computer-generated imagery (CGI) in groundbreaking ways with films like \"Jurassic Park\" (1993). His use of special effects has often set industry benchmarks.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
